      "label": "Interim Boundary Commission for Northern Ireland, Report (1967): figures for existing seats",
      "note": "The Commission (appointed by warrant of 31 January 1967) gave population and electorate figures for the six existing 1929 seats it reviewed: Antrim 61,431 / 33,347; Bann Side 25,143 / 16,062; Carrick 70,701 / 41,669; South Antrim 59,133 / 37,095; Mid Down 74,623 / 45,754; North Down population uncertain (64,450 or 46,450) / electorate 30,286. The other 42 seats were not reviewed. Prepared as feature properties ibc1967_population and ibc1967_electorate in data/review-inputs/electorates-2026-10-31/stormont-1929-ibc1967.json, not yet in the map tiles."
    },
    {
      "label": "House of Commons (Method of Voting and Redistribution of Seats) Act (Northern Ireland) 1929 (19 Geo. 5 c. 5)",
      "url": "https://www.thegazette.co.uk/Belfast/issue/408/page/453",
      "note": "Replaced the multi-member PR constituencies of 1921-29 with 48 single-member territorial seats elected by plurality, plus the four-seat Queen's University. Royal Assent notified in the Belfast Gazette, issue 408, 19 Apr 1929, page 453. Not printed on legislation.gov.uk (repealed)."
    },
    {
      "label": "PRONI CAB/9/B/13/2: Redistribution: House of Commons (Method of Voting and Redistribution of Seats) Bill (Northern Ireland) 1929 (1910-1934)",
      "url": "https://civgraph.net/proni/CAB/9/B/13/2",
      "note": "Cabinet Secretariat file on the 1929 Bill, with electoral alterations in Omagh in 1934 (PRONI eCatalogue description; open). Archival source for the background to this map."
    },
    {
      "label": "PRONI CAB/9/B/13/1: Redistribution: abolition of proportional representation and the redistribution of electoral areas in Northern Ireland (1921-1927)",
      "url": "https://civgraph.net/proni/CAB/9/B/13/1",
      "note": "Cabinet Secretariat file (PRONI eCatalogue description; open). Covers the run-up to the 1929 redistribution and the 1923-24 local government electoral areas."
